{%- doc -%}
  Prints the name to show for a product: the `custom.display_name` metafield when
  it is set, otherwise the Shopify product title.

  The backend keeps one product per colourway with a full title ("Crosspoint MTN
  Scape Dusk Orange") so admin, search and swatch labels stay unambiguous, while the
  storefront shows the model name like spyoptic.com ("Crosspoint").

  @param {product} product - product to read the name from

  @example
  {%- capture name -%}{%- render 'spy-display-name', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign spy_display_name = product.metafields.custom.display_name.value | strip
  if spy_display_name == blank
    assign spy_display_name = product.title
  endif
  echo spy_display_name
-%}
